  "body": "### Summary\n\nCapture on the Mac, with the LOT-001 (#38) kit (`tooling/fixtures/`), two page states LOT-038 needs to locate the MPStorage thread:\n- the MP list when the storage thread is **not on page 1** (page 2 or later);\n- the \"destiné\" page that legacy treats as a dead end (LOT-038 spec, quirk 18).\n\n### Scope\n\n- A logged-in MP list where the MPStorage thread sits on page 2 or later. Capture page 1 (without it) and the page that holds it, as a read-only GET.\n- The \"destiné\" page, as legacy reaches it when it looks for the storage thread. Read the legacy `MPStorage.m` find path (at `2440d79`, see the LOT-004 spec) for the exact URL, and never guess it.\n\nRules: anonymize every free-text field. Never hand-build the state in the cloud (LESSONS 36). Add a legacy oracle when a parser consumes it (LOT-002 (#39)..005 tooling). One PR per batch of captures.\n\n### Wanted by\n\nLOT-038 (#65), whose body names both states as *pending capture*, and through it LOT-052 (#78).\n\n### Depends on\n\n—\n\n### Owner / session\n\n— (ready; `host: mac`)\n\n### Source\n\nLOT-038 issue body (steward rewrite, 2026-10-29). Restart plan on #166.",
