   "body": "### Capture result (mac/capture-batch, run 9, PR #400) — partial\nCorpus ids: `R96b`, `R95k`.\n- **\"destiné\" for the storage thread** (`R96b`, legacy oracle `LOT-004/R96b.oracle.json`, `mpstorage-page`): user2 opening user1's storage thread with legacy's read URL (`MPStorage.m:766`) answers 200 with the `.hop` \"Ce message ne vous est pas destiné, désolé\", as `RA5`.\n- **Storage row on page 2 or later: not captured.** user1's storage row is row 42 of 50 on page 1 (`R95k`); pushing it to page 2 needs about 9 newer conversations, and HFR allows one new MP per account per 60 minutes (`W11x`); user2 has no storage thread. Replying in user1's real conversations to bump them is out of scope.\n\nThis issue stays open for that state. A later Mac run could create ~9 throwaway threads between the two accounts over ~5 hours (alternating senders), then delete them; that needs the operator's go. Decision needed (operator)\n",
   "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
